{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having really bad abdominal pain for about a week, and last night I had over 20 watery bowel movements. It feels like my Crohn’s is flaring up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned Crohn’s—can you tell me more about your history with it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I had most of my colon removed years ago. I’ve tried several medications, but nothing’s worked long-term. I’m on steroids now and had to increase my dose a bit last week because I felt worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. Your labs show your white blood cell count is elevated, which supports an active flare. We’ve also started you on IV fluids and gave you some pain medication in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. The pain is mostly in my lower left side and back, and it moves toward my stomach. Heat helps a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your exam shows tenderness in the upper quadrants, but no signs of a surgical emergency. We’re going to start you on IV steroids to help calm the inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s what usually helps. But I’m worried—could this be something else, like an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. We tested your stool for C. diff, and it came back negative. We’re also checking for parasites and viruses, but so far no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I’ve also noticed some blood when I wipe—should I be concerned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely from irritation due to frequent bowel movements. We didn’t see blood in your stool sample, so it’s probably not coming from deep in the intestine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about the chest X-ray I had? Anything show up there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s a small shadow at the base of your left lung. It could be early pneumonia or just some collapsed lung tissue from shallow breathing due to pain. You don’t have a fever or cough, so we think it’s likely benign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. But if you develop a fever or cough, let us know immediately. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. What’s the plan for my pain and diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you IV methylprednisone three times a day. For pain, you’ll get Dilaudid and Tylenol as needed. We’ve also added cholestyramine to help with the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never taken cholestyramine before. What does it do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps bind bile acids that can worsen diarrhea in people who’ve had bowel surgery. It’s often helpful in cases like yours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, okay. And I’m still taking loperamide, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-05-20 15:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing your usual loperamide. We’ll watch your bowel movements closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your symptoms are improving—your bowel movements have slowed and are more formed. That’s a good sign the treatment is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I feel a bit better. Less cramping. What about those test results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CMV test came back negative, which is great—no viral infection. Stool tests for parasites and other pathogens were also negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s definitely a Crohn’s flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all signs point to that. No infection found, and your history and symptoms match perfectly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Can I start eating again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to advance your diet to regular food today. Start slowly and let us know if you feel bloated or nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. And the IV steroids—will I stay on those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll transition you to oral prednisone today. You’ll take 40 mg daily for now, then discuss tapering with your gastroenterologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought I was on 25 mg when I came in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were, but because this is a significant flare, we’re increasing it temporarily to get better control before starting the taper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. What about my kidney stone? I had one before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We didn’t do a new scan this time, but given your history, we recommend you follow up with urology to monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do that. Any other follow-up I need?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-05-21 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you should see your primary care doctor to review steroid precautions—like bone health and infection prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. You’re eating normally, pain is controlled, and your bowels are stable. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take prednisone 40 mg daily, omeprazole once a day, loperamide as needed, cholestyramine twice a day, and Percocet for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll follow up with GI soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, within the next week. They’ll help adjust your steroid taper and long-term plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep an eye on your symptoms, and call if you develop fever, worsening pain, or breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-05-22 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications before you leave."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-05-20 15:22:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-05-22 17:13:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of ileocolonic Crohn’s disease status post subtotal colectomy and ileorectal anastomosis, steroid-dependent and refractory to multiple biologics, was admitted for worsening abdominal pain and diarrhea consistent with a disease flare. He reported over 20 watery bowel movements in one night and increased abdominal pain, particularly in the left lower quadrant. Labs showed leukocytosis with a left shift, but stool studies were negative for C. diff, parasites, and CMV. He was treated with IV methylprednisone, transitioned to oral prednisone, and started on cholestyramine for diarrhea control. Pain was managed with Dilaudid and Tylenol, then switched to oral Percocet. His symptoms improved, diet was advanced, and he was discharged home on a temporary increased steroid dose with plans to follow up with gastroenterology for tapering and urology for kidney stone monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine with large intestine",
      "Acquired absence of intestine (large) (small)",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Displacement of lumbar intervertebral disc without myelopathy",
      "Unspecified cataract",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Other B-complex deficiencies",
      "Nonspecific reaction to tuberculin skin test without active tuberculosis"
    ]
  }
}
